---
description: Commit and push completed work to origin without waiting to be asked
alwaysApply: true
---

# Always push

When you finish a change the user asked for, commit it and `git push` to the tracked remote.

- Do this even if they did not say "commit" or "push".
- Never force-push, never skip hooks, never amend a commit that is already on the remote.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets.
- Use a short commit message that says why, matching this repo's style.
- After pushing, mention that it is on the remote (Render deploys from GitHub).
